  "raw_label": "appellant_won",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Jitender Bansal Proprietor Of Dk ... vs Spg Consumer Products Private Limited & ... on 16 July, 2024 Author: Jasmeet Singh Bench: Jasmeet Singh $~7 * In The High Court Of Delhi At New Delhi + Arb.P. 746/2024 Jitender Bansal Proprietor Of Dk Enterpr Through: Mr. Anish Roy, Tiwari, Mr. Din Dileep Rajpuroh Agarwal, Advoca versus SPG CONSUMER PRODUCTS PRIVATE LIMITED & Through: Mr. Bikram Sing Raghav Bundila Agarwala, Advoc CORAM: HON'BLE MR. JUSTICE JASMEET SINGH ORDER % 16.07.2024 1.",
    "facts": "This is a petition filed under Section 11(5) and (6) of the Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996 seeking appointment of the Sole Arbitrator to adjudicate the disputes between the parties. 2. The respondent had appointed the petitioner as Super Distributor of South and West Delhi vide Agreement dated 27.01.2022. As per the petitioner, the respondent had supplied edible oils which were of inferior quality and had failed quality tests of Food Laboratory of Department of Food Safety, GNCTD which was informed to the petitioner by the Department of Food Safety. 3. M/s Bedi Trading Company withheld the payments of the petitioner due to quality issue of the edible oil. Since there were disputes between the parties, the respondent invoked the bank guarantees of the petitioner. The petitioner approached DLSA and applied for pre-institution mediation which was declared as non-starter. Thereafter, the petitioner filed suit bearing No. CS (COMM) 740/2023 before the Commercial Courts, District and Sessions Judge, Central District, wherein the respondent took an objection under Section 8 of Arbitration and Conciliation Act, 1996. On 22.01.2023, the said objection was allowed.",
    "arguments": "Mr. Bikram Singh, learned counsel appears for the respondent and states that he has no objection if the [LEAKAGE_MASK]."
  },
